    {
      "id": "2122220308799316072",
      "author": "elonmusk",
      "author_name": "Elon Musk",
      "author_avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2053244804520427520/m8mdWZCG_200x200.jpg",
      "author_verified": true,
      "author_verified_type": "individual",
      "created_at_utc": "2026-11-16T06:48:45.000Z",
      "created_at_shanghai": "2026-11-16 14:48:45",
      "type": "引用",
      "type_label": "引用",
      "text": "The amount of energy we harness for civilization from the Sun will obviously ultimately round up to 100% of all energy. That math is obvious and trivial.",
      "quote": {
        "author": "XFreeze",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1876785200010539008/2_HFJjq9_200x200.jpg",
        "created_at_shanghai": "2026-11-16 12:35:06",
        "created_at_utc": "2026-11-16T04:35:06.000Z",
        "id": "2122186676164587648",
        "images": [
          "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HXOFh9fa4AArnDe.jpg?name=small"
        ],
        "media": [
          {
            "height": 675,
            "type": "photo",
            "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HXOFh9fa4AArnDe.jpg?name=small",
            "width": 1200
          }
        ],
        "name": "X Freeze",
        "text": "Years ago, Elon Musk predicted:\n\n“Solar electricity will become by far the biggest source of power for civilization”\n\nToday, we're watching that vision become reality\n\nIn 2015, solar generated just 256 TWh of electricity globally\n\nA decade later, annual solar generation has surpassed 2,700 TWh\n\nThat's more than a 10X increase in just ten years\n\nSolar also accounted for 83% of the growth in global electricity demand during the first half of 2025\n\nAnd renewables have now overtaken coal in global electricity generation\n\nWhat Elon Musk envisioned years ago is unfolding right in front of us\n\nThe Sun is a gigantic fusion reactor in space, delivering more energy to Earth in a single hour than humanity consumes in an entire year\n\nWe're still capturing only a tiny fraction of it\n\nSolar generation is accelerating, battery storage is expanding, and the world is moving toward a future of abundant, sustainable energy\n\nAnd this transformation is only getting started",
        "url": "https://x.com/XFreeze/status/2122186676164587648",
        "verified": true,
        "verified_type": "individual"
      },
      "retweet": null,
      "reply_to": "",
      "engagement": {
        "bookmarks": 30,
        "likes": 550,
        "quotes": 12,
        "replies": 152,
        "retweets": 83,
        "views": 307271
      },
      "url": "https://x.com/elonmusk/status/2122220308799316072",
      "images": [],
      "media": [],
      "enriched": true
    },
    {
      "id": "2122203324460265943",
      "author": "elonmusk",
      "author_name": "Elon Musk",
      "author_avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2053244804520427520/m8mdWZCG_200x200.jpg",
      "author_verified": true,
      "author_verified_type": "individual",
      "created_at_utc": "2026-11-16T05:41:15.000Z",
      "created_at_shanghai": "2026-11-16 13:41:15",
      "type": "引用",
      "type_label": "引用",
      "text": "Yup",
      "quote": {
        "author": "XFreeze",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1876785200010539008/2_HFJjq9_200x200.jpg",
        "created_at_shanghai": "2026-11-16 13:04:06",
        "created_at_utc": "2026-11-16T05:04:06.000Z",
        "id": "2122193972722573371",
        "images": [
          "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HXOMKmBbQAADlGZ.jpg?name=small"
        ],
        "media": [
          {
            "height": 1800,
            "type": "photo",
            "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HXOMKmBbQAADlGZ.jpg?name=small",
            "width": 3200
          }
        ],
        "name": "X Freeze",
        "text": "In 2014, NASA awarded Boeing $4.2 BILLION to develop Starliner\n\nSpaceX received just $2.6 BILLION for Crew Dragon\n\nNow look at the results:\n\n• Boeing Starliner: Just one crewed flight and got two astronauts stuck on the ISS for over 9 months in space before SpaceX sent Dragon to rescue them\n\n• SpaceX Crew Dragon: 21 crewed missions since 2020, carrying astronauts to orbit for NASA and private customers, saving NASA billions of dollars\n\nBoeing received $1.6 BILLION more in the original NASA contract\n\nYet SpaceX ended up bringing Boeing's own astronauts back to Earth",
        "url": "https://x.com/XFreeze/status/2122193972722573371",
        "verified": true,
        "verified_type": "individual"
      },
      "retweet": null,
